1
00:00:00,166 --> 00:00:01,166
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,166 --> 00:00:02,166
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,166 --> 00:00:03,733
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,733 --> 00:00:06,933
[Episode 9]

5
00:00:20,767 --> 00:00:22,467
You startled me!

6
00:00:24,622 --> 00:00:27,666
- What are you doing?
- Huh? What is it?

7
00:00:28,382 --> 00:00:33,233
I feel like I said something important
and heard something even more important.

8
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:38,499
Wow, I never knew there was
honey tea in the break room.

9
00:00:40,101 --> 00:00:43,050
You don't usually drink like that.

10
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,455
You should've gone home
and become one with your bed.

11
00:00:45,455 --> 00:00:47,069
Why'd you come in on the weekend?

12
00:00:47,069 --> 00:00:50,254
Why did you come in, then?

13
00:00:50,254 --> 00:00:55,233
Me? Are you asking me?
Are you genuinely curious?

14
00:00:56,057 --> 00:01:00,499
Then shall I give you a sincere answer?

15
00:01:01,202 --> 00:01:03,233
"Look into the unusual death
in Hyeonsa-dong."

16
00:01:03,233 --> 00:01:06,433
"Pull a list of the punks recently released
who didn't serve enough time."

17
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:08,142
You're making my head spin.

18
00:01:08,142 --> 00:01:11,854
My head's already not exactly
in working order.

19
00:01:11,854 --> 00:01:14,986
[Violent Crimes Team 2]
And that's not all. See this?

20
00:01:14,986 --> 00:01:17,466
Endless Kingfisher material?

21
00:01:17,466 --> 00:01:18,688
This is why I'm...

22
00:01:18,688 --> 00:01:21,166
Need to take the exam again?

23
00:01:24,754 --> 00:01:27,788
[Kingfisher Case Files]
Let's see. Today...

24
00:01:27,788 --> 00:01:29,134
[Haegong-dong Gosiwon Case]
Oh, Haegong-dong Gosiwon?

25
00:01:29,134 --> 00:01:30,370
Oh, this is that case.

26
00:01:30,370 --> 00:01:32,958
Kingfisher's last case before disappearing.

27
00:01:34,066 --> 00:01:36,433
I think I'm finally getting somewhere.

28
00:01:39,659 --> 00:01:41,578
[Haegong-dong Case Overview]

29
00:01:42,588 --> 00:01:44,781
[With seven-year-old Yeon Cheol present]
Huh? What's this?

30
00:01:44,781 --> 00:01:47,617
There was a seven-year-old child
at the scene?

31
00:01:47,617 --> 00:01:51,446
But there's a side of him people don't know.

32
00:01:51,446 --> 00:01:54,646
A punk who shot a dad dead

33
00:01:54,646 --> 00:01:58,262
right in front of his seven-year-old son.

34
00:01:58,262 --> 00:01:59,958
<i>Actually, I know.</i>

35
00:01:59,958 --> 00:02:03,366
I'm telling you, I saw Kingfisher.

36
00:02:04,433 --> 00:02:09,918
I was there at the Haegong-dong
Gosiwon case that day.

37
00:02:09,918 --> 00:02:12,233
- Ah!
- Oh, you startled me!

38
00:02:14,632 --> 00:02:18,122
Bo Na, you didn't answer,
so I left a message.

39
00:02:18,122 --> 00:02:19,936
<i>Did you just see it?</i>

40
00:02:19,936 --> 00:02:21,432
You pulled another prank on me?

41
00:02:21,432 --> 00:02:23,233
Oh, jeez.

42
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:26,822
I figured you'd be home
since it's the weekend.

43
00:02:26,822 --> 00:02:29,250
Was I being rude?

44
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:31,478
Should I wait out here?

45
00:02:31,478 --> 00:02:34,699
You can wait inside if you don't mind.

46
00:02:36,399 --> 00:02:37,433
[Bo Na]

47
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:38,514
[Speakerphone]

48
00:02:38,514 --> 00:02:41,433
Bo Na, is it okay if I do that?

49
00:02:43,166 --> 00:02:45,442
Listen carefully.

50
00:02:45,442 --> 00:02:47,655
<i>If you say even one useless word,</i>

51
00:02:47,655 --> 00:02:50,570
you'll die by my hand.

52
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:53,470
That's hurtful. You don't trust me?

53
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:58,276
Back then and now, ever since "that day."

54
00:02:58,276 --> 00:03:02,298
If you don't want to die,
you'd better remember what I said.

55
00:03:02,298 --> 00:03:04,866
Thanks for welcoming me, Bo Na.

56
00:03:05,626 --> 00:03:08,433
Come quickly. I miss you.

57
00:03:11,510 --> 00:03:13,210
Please come on in.

58
00:03:21,288 --> 00:03:24,366
Congratulations. You're pregnant.

59
00:03:24,366 --> 00:03:26,306
You're five weeks along.

60
00:03:26,306 --> 00:03:27,306
[Four Years Ago, "That Day"]

61
00:03:27,306 --> 00:03:30,194
Right here, do you see this little bean?

62
00:03:30,194 --> 00:03:31,606
That's the gestational sac.

63
00:03:31,606 --> 00:03:33,070
The gestational sac?

64
00:03:33,070 --> 00:03:35,299
Yeah.

65
00:03:35,299 --> 00:03:36,958
[Prenatal Care Booklet]

66
00:03:36,958 --> 00:03:39,786
<i>You're still in the early stages,
so you need to be extra careful, okay?</i>

67
00:03:39,786 --> 00:03:43,726
<i>Avoid running, strenuous exercise,
and lifting heavy objects.</i>

68
00:03:43,726 --> 00:03:45,478
<i>It's also best to avoid
rushing up and down stairs</i>

69
00:03:45,478 --> 00:03:50,210
or making sudden movements
like sitting down and standing up quickly.

70
00:03:50,210 --> 00:03:54,010
Most importantly, try to stay relaxed.

71
00:03:54,010 --> 00:03:57,266
Stress can have a negative effect.

72
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:03,233
[Calls]

73
00:04:03,233 --> 00:04:05,299
[My Santa]

74
00:04:08,599 --> 00:04:10,733
[Incoming Call, My Santa]

75
00:04:10,733 --> 00:04:12,833
[My Santa]

76
00:04:14,238 --> 00:04:15,238
Tae Seong.

77
00:04:15,238 --> 00:04:17,326
<i>Yeah, honey. Did you have lunch?</i>

78
00:04:17,326 --> 00:04:19,146
Of course. Look at the time. I ate ages ago.

79
00:04:19,146 --> 00:04:20,206
What about you, Tae Seong?

80
00:04:20,206 --> 00:04:22,002
<i>I'm on my way to get something to eat.</i>

81
00:04:22,002 --> 00:04:24,594
<i>I just finished an interview.</i>

82
00:04:24,594 --> 00:04:26,142
You must be starving.

83
00:04:26,142 --> 00:04:28,099
<i>What's wrong with your voice?</i>

84
00:04:28,845 --> 00:04:30,545
<i>Are you sick?</i>

85
00:04:32,030 --> 00:04:35,099
No, I'm perfectly fine. Why do you ask?

86
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:38,978
Are you going to be late today?

87
00:04:38,978 --> 00:04:42,610
<i>Even if I leave right after lunch,</i>

88
00:04:42,610 --> 00:04:44,150
<i>I'll probably have to stop by the office,</i>

89
00:04:44,150 --> 00:04:46,598
<i>so it'll be evening by the time I get there.</i>

90
00:04:46,598 --> 00:04:48,390
I wish you could come early.

91
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:50,122
[Prenatal Care Booklet]
So we can have dinner together.

92
00:04:50,122 --> 00:04:52,498
I have something to show you.

93
00:04:52,498 --> 00:04:56,666
<i>Of course, I'll come early.
I'll wrap things up and fly home.</i>

94
00:05:07,374 --> 00:05:09,997
Have you figured out
what you're going to do next?

95
00:05:09,997 --> 00:05:10,997
Not really.

96
00:05:10,997 --> 00:05:14,678
I was thinking of opening
a little shop with my severance pay,

97
00:05:14,678 --> 00:05:16,626
but I don't have anything specific in mind.

98
00:05:16,626 --> 00:05:18,582
If I had my way,

99
00:05:18,582 --> 00:05:22,714
I'd like to spend the rest of my life
looking at beautiful things.

100
00:05:22,714 --> 00:05:25,933
Then you should open a flower shop.
Flowers are beautiful.

101
00:05:27,642 --> 00:05:30,306
Hey, wow!

102
00:05:30,306 --> 00:05:35,038
Even Yoo Bo Na knows flowers are pretty.
Feels like a whole different era.

103
00:05:35,038 --> 00:05:38,430
Well, I guess the world has changed.

104
00:05:38,430 --> 00:05:40,590
Your world has.

105
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:43,466
Well, you look so much brighter too.

106
00:05:43,466 --> 00:05:45,699
I guess married life
is treating you well, huh?

107
00:05:55,402 --> 00:06:00,399
But once the baby arrives,
does the world really change?

108
00:06:05,534 --> 00:06:07,466
Are you planning to have a baby?

109
00:06:10,274 --> 00:06:12,406
I can't quite explain how I feel.

110
00:06:12,406 --> 00:06:14,330
It scares me too.

111
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:19,494
The word "mom" just feels
so far away from me.

112
00:06:19,494 --> 00:06:21,258
You're worrying about nothing.

113
00:06:21,258 --> 00:06:23,130
You'll still be you after you become a mom.

114
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:26,338
"Your world won't change.
It just gets bigger."

115
00:06:26,338 --> 00:06:29,233
That's what my grandma always used to say.

116
00:06:30,058 --> 00:06:32,366
And that's what I believed too.

117
00:06:34,694 --> 00:06:36,814
Do you think I can really do this?

118
00:06:36,814 --> 00:06:38,866
You're already doing a great job.

119
00:06:39,934 --> 00:06:44,899
You've got herbal tea in front of you
instead of your beloved coffee.

120
00:06:48,522 --> 00:06:50,126
Don't worry.

121
00:06:50,126 --> 00:06:52,846
Your world has already changed once.

122
00:06:52,846 --> 00:06:57,666
It's only going to get bigger
and stronger from now on.

123
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:14,942
- Yes, Team Leader.
- <i>Oh, Director Yoo.</i>

124
00:07:14,942 --> 00:07:18,154
The Yeon Chang Bok meeting today
has fallen through.

125
00:07:18,154 --> 00:07:19,833
Ugh, that darn punk...

126
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:23,466
He made a move
before Manager Go could do anything.

127
00:07:23,466 --> 00:07:24,742
Yeah.

128
00:07:24,742 --> 00:07:28,066
I'm chasing him right now.
He's getting away in a taxi.

129
00:07:28,066 --> 00:07:29,586
He moved faster than we expected.

130
00:07:29,586 --> 00:07:34,646
Who knew he'd change his mind
the second he got to the hospital?

131
00:07:34,646 --> 00:07:36,899
If we lose him now,

132
00:07:36,899 --> 00:07:40,822
I don't think we'll get
another chance to catch him easily.

133
00:07:40,822 --> 00:07:44,099
We need to revise the scenario. I'll go.

134
00:07:44,099 --> 00:07:46,299
Keep me updated on his route.

135
00:08:54,766 --> 00:08:56,099
What did you bring?

136
00:08:56,099 --> 00:08:57,531
Forget that. The money!

137
00:08:57,531 --> 00:08:59,231
Here.

138
00:09:10,658 --> 00:09:11,866
- Team Leader.
- Yeah?

139
00:09:11,866 --> 00:09:14,126
[Haegong-dong Gosiwon]
Yeon Chang Bok's mom and son are here.

140
00:09:14,126 --> 00:09:15,266
A son?

141
00:09:15,266 --> 00:09:18,282
The newborn his mom was holding
when he was arrested.

142
00:09:18,282 --> 00:09:21,106
Yeah, I'll wait until they leave.

143
00:09:21,106 --> 00:09:23,086
The police are about to storm in.

144
00:09:23,086 --> 00:09:24,338
<i>This doesn't look good.</i>

145
00:09:24,338 --> 00:09:26,294
Not in front of the kid.

146
00:09:26,294 --> 00:09:27,994
I'll just wait.

147
00:09:30,479 --> 00:09:31,998
Surprise!

148
00:09:31,998 --> 00:09:34,299
Hi, my friend.

149
00:09:50,582 --> 00:09:52,146
- It came out again.
- Right?

150
00:09:52,146 --> 00:09:53,670
Isn't it awesome?

151
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:55,926
- Another one!
- There it is again.

152
00:09:55,926 --> 00:09:57,862
Honey, you're back?

153
00:09:57,862 --> 00:09:58,862
Mommy!

154
00:09:58,862 --> 00:10:01,462
More and more toys
keep coming out of the doll.

155
00:10:01,462 --> 00:10:02,662
Yeah?

156
00:10:02,662 --> 00:10:06,166
Sergei brought another gift for Yul.

157
00:10:07,122 --> 00:10:08,690
You should've told me you were coming.

158
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:10,566
Surprise!

159
00:10:12,010 --> 00:10:13,866
Hi, my friend.

160
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:16,762
It's here, it's here!

161
00:10:16,762 --> 00:10:19,299
- What's here?
- Chicken! Chicken's here!

162
00:10:19,299 --> 00:10:23,374
I think your husband's jealous of us.

163
00:10:23,374 --> 00:10:26,333
Behave yourself.

164
00:10:27,433 --> 00:10:29,542
[Tae Seong Chicken]
I didn't have anything proper to serve him,

165
00:10:29,542 --> 00:10:32,030
so I asked Sun Il for a favor.

166
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:34,646
I could've just taken him out for dinner.

167
00:10:34,646 --> 00:10:37,233
You're not feeling well.
Why go through all that trouble?

168
00:10:37,233 --> 00:10:41,833
No, I'm fine. I told you I wanted
to see your Russian friend too.

169
00:10:43,902 --> 00:10:46,334
I didn't know he was that kind of man.

170
00:10:46,334 --> 00:10:48,262
Didn't I tell you he was a man?

171
00:10:48,262 --> 00:10:49,918
I think I did.

172
00:10:49,918 --> 00:10:52,166
Yeah, you said he was a man.

173
00:10:52,899 --> 00:10:56,170
You just didn't say he was that good-looking.

174
00:10:56,170 --> 00:10:58,302
- Huh?
- What?

175
00:10:58,302 --> 00:10:59,886
You think he's a good-looking man?

176
00:10:59,886 --> 00:11:01,146
He's pretty handsome.

177
00:11:01,146 --> 00:11:03,066
You, seriously...

178
00:11:04,534 --> 00:11:06,589
Let's go eat too.

179
00:11:11,410 --> 00:11:14,286
Korean fried chicken really is the best.

180
00:11:14,286 --> 00:11:15,642
It's so good.

181
00:11:15,642 --> 00:11:18,266
I'm glad it suits your taste.

182
00:11:18,266 --> 00:11:20,734
But Sergei...

183
00:11:20,734 --> 00:11:24,182
Just call me Seul Gi. That's easier.

184
00:11:24,182 --> 00:11:25,310
I'm good with that too.

185
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:27,266
Oh, alright.

186
00:11:28,834 --> 00:11:33,178
Seul Gi, I heard you were born in Russia.

187
00:11:33,178 --> 00:11:34,826
But your Korean is really good.

188
00:11:34,826 --> 00:11:38,410
My mama is Korean.

189
00:11:38,410 --> 00:11:42,499
And I got used to the language
from playing with Bo Na since we were kids.

190
00:11:45,998 --> 00:11:48,834
Yeah, we lived in the same
neighborhood back then.

191
00:11:48,834 --> 00:11:52,662
I think I first met Bo Na when we were eight.

192
00:11:52,662 --> 00:11:55,658
Right after you moved to Russia, remember?

193
00:11:55,658 --> 00:11:57,350
You're right.

194
00:11:57,350 --> 00:12:00,133
So you've known each other for a long time.

195
00:12:00,890 --> 00:12:03,154
We have.

196
00:12:03,154 --> 00:12:05,682
By the way, are you okay, honey?

197
00:12:05,682 --> 00:12:09,133
Well, he came home so wasted
last night that he blacked out.

198
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:10,166
- You must be exhausted.
- No...

199
00:12:10,166 --> 00:12:12,386
- Can you really eat this right now?
- No, I'm fine. I'm really fine.

200
00:12:12,386 --> 00:12:16,062
I just enjoy hearing about your past.

201
00:12:16,062 --> 00:12:17,342
- It's good.
- I'm fine.

202
00:12:17,342 --> 00:12:18,762
Well, it's...

203
00:12:18,762 --> 00:12:20,486
When I first met Bo Na,

204
00:12:20,486 --> 00:12:26,154
I said in Korean, "Hi, I'm Sergei."

205
00:12:26,154 --> 00:12:27,810
And she goes, "Seul Gi?"

206
00:12:27,810 --> 00:12:30,294
"No, Sergei."

207
00:12:30,294 --> 00:12:33,666
"Ah! No Seul Gi?"

208
00:12:38,990 --> 00:12:44,242
From that day on,
I was just "No Seul Gi" to Bo Na.

209
00:12:44,242 --> 00:12:46,499
So that's the story behind your nickname.

210
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:50,030
Yul, chew this slowly and thoroughly, okay?

211
00:12:50,030 --> 00:12:51,690
Mommy, you eat some too.

212
00:12:51,690 --> 00:12:53,499
Is this for me?

213
00:12:54,466 --> 00:12:55,950
It's good. Thank you.

214
00:12:55,950 --> 00:12:58,054
Bo Na, are you eating chicken?

215
00:12:58,054 --> 00:12:59,894
You never used to like chicken.

216
00:12:59,894 --> 00:13:01,014
I do now.

217
00:13:01,014 --> 00:13:03,658
Really? That's interesting.

218
00:13:03,658 --> 00:13:06,138
You used to hate the smell of chicken...

219
00:13:06,138 --> 00:13:08,286
Oh, chicken porridge!

220
00:13:08,286 --> 00:13:10,499
You didn't like chicken porridge either.

221
00:13:11,866 --> 00:13:13,810
- Huh?
- Back then, I did.

222
00:13:13,810 --> 00:13:18,433
It seems there are still a lot of things
you don't know about Bo Na.

223
00:13:19,722 --> 00:13:22,199
Or does she just not tell you
much about herself?

224
00:13:25,222 --> 00:13:29,599
When Bo Na was in school,
some mean kids used to play pranks on her.

225
00:13:29,599 --> 00:13:33,606
They'd secretly dunk
her chicken in muddy water,

226
00:13:33,606 --> 00:13:37,530
or pour strong whiskey into her chicken soup.

227
00:13:37,530 --> 00:13:39,799
So sometimes...

228
00:13:40,654 --> 00:13:43,133
things got physical.

229
00:13:44,606 --> 00:13:47,570
Bo Na was pretty tough back then.

230
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:49,733
Hey, you don't need to bring that up.

231
00:13:49,733 --> 00:13:55,278
In Korean, we'd say "no mercy."

232
00:13:55,278 --> 00:13:58,594
Bo Na is very self-assured
and clear about what she wants in everything.

233
00:13:58,594 --> 00:14:00,799
She knows exactly what's right and wrong.

234
00:14:01,906 --> 00:14:03,386
- Is that so?
- Yeah.

235
00:14:03,386 --> 00:14:06,618
And Bo Na eats chicken just fine now.
She even likes chicken porridge.

236
00:14:06,618 --> 00:14:09,399
Food tastes different depending on

237
00:14:09,399 --> 00:14:14,314
who you eat it with
and what memories it holds, right?

238
00:14:14,314 --> 00:14:16,438
Oh, I see.

239
00:14:16,438 --> 00:14:18,790
I may not have known
the Bo Na from childhood,

240
00:14:18,790 --> 00:14:21,010
but I know who she is now.

241
00:14:21,010 --> 00:14:25,194
Because what matters
is the present, not the past.

242
00:14:25,194 --> 00:14:26,894
Isn't it?

243
00:14:28,010 --> 00:14:32,142
I was curious what kind of man
Bo Na would end up with.

244
00:14:32,142 --> 00:14:33,954
Looks like she found a good one.

245
00:14:33,954 --> 00:14:37,666
Oh, no. I'm the one who got lucky enough
to meet an amazing woman.

246
00:14:41,610 --> 00:14:43,033
He is so tired now.

247
00:14:43,033 --> 00:14:46,834
Let's finish up and go have some tea, okay?

248
00:14:46,834 --> 00:14:48,534
Alright.

249
00:14:56,050 --> 00:14:57,514
We'll just have tea and come right back.

250
00:14:57,514 --> 00:14:59,538
I'll be back soon, Yul, okay?

251
00:14:59,538 --> 00:15:00,538
Take your time.

252
00:15:00,538 --> 00:15:03,599
You two must have a lot
to catch up on after all this time.

253
00:15:04,746 --> 00:15:07,154
Thanks for the great chicken
and the wonderful conversation.

254
00:15:07,154 --> 00:15:09,609
- Let's catch up again soon.
- Okay.

255
00:15:12,734 --> 00:15:14,754
Goodbye! Little Yul.

256
00:15:14,754 --> 00:15:16,933
Goodbye.

257
00:15:20,478 --> 00:15:23,033
Goodbye, Tae Seong.

258
00:16:04,829 --> 00:16:07,830
Oh, Bo Na, calm down.

259
00:16:07,830 --> 00:16:10,533
I told you not to show your face
in front of me again, didn't I?

260
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:15,399
Just as I thought,
those two are your Achilles' heels.

261
00:16:16,562 --> 00:16:20,454
Looks like my warning that day
wasn't strong enough.

262
00:16:20,454 --> 00:16:25,966
Having something to protect
is a fatal weakness for killers like us.

263
00:16:33,170 --> 00:16:34,370
Okay.

264
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:37,250
I'm not coming back.

265
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:39,166
I promise you.

266
00:16:39,166 --> 00:16:41,790
That's your second warning.

267
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,599
No third chance.

268
00:16:45,314 --> 00:16:47,014
Get lost.

269
00:16:47,982 --> 00:16:50,133
I really meant it.

270
00:16:54,058 --> 00:16:56,999
You seem to have found a good guy.

271
00:17:35,233 --> 00:17:36,599
[Four Years Ago, "That Day"]
No way!

272
00:17:36,599 --> 00:17:39,762
It seems like Yeon Chang Bok escaped
from the hospital while in medical custody.

273
00:17:39,762 --> 00:17:41,842
Yeon Chang Bok?

274
00:17:41,842 --> 00:17:43,733
Yeon Chang Bok...

275
00:17:45,150 --> 00:17:46,664
Oh, that guy...

276
00:17:46,664 --> 00:17:50,226
The aggravated sex offender who broke into
a home and threatened the family?

277
00:17:50,226 --> 00:17:52,049
The lowest of the low.

278
00:17:52,049 --> 00:17:55,098
He pointed the knife at the victim's baby,
not even the victim herself.

279
00:17:55,098 --> 00:17:57,526
The mom eventually
took her own life a few months later.

280
00:17:57,526 --> 00:17:59,982
Right, you covered that case too, didn't you?

281
00:17:59,982 --> 00:18:01,330
Yeah, for a day.

282
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:06,426
The day Yeon Chang Bok's mom protested
outside the courthouse for leniency.

283
00:18:06,426 --> 00:18:09,478
Yeah, I accompanied the mom
and followed her to her house.

284
00:18:09,478 --> 00:18:11,426
And I even saw Yeon Chang Bok's son.

285
00:18:11,426 --> 00:18:15,099
Someone like that should be
taken out by Kingfisher.

286
00:18:15,810 --> 00:18:17,633
So, are you a Kingfisher fan too, Mr. Nam?

287
00:18:17,633 --> 00:18:21,218
Oh, a lot of reporters secretly
support him, actually.

288
00:18:21,218 --> 00:18:22,758
Hold on.

289
00:18:22,758 --> 00:18:25,599
At this rate, won't Kingfisher
find this punk first?

290
00:18:25,599 --> 00:18:29,033
He's always a step ahead of the cops.

291
00:18:29,033 --> 00:18:32,686
Honestly, that might be better than
getting caught by the police.

292
00:18:32,686 --> 00:18:35,626
Sorry, Mr. Nam, but I think
I should go into the office alone.

293
00:18:35,626 --> 00:18:38,066
What? Why?

294
00:20:41,310 --> 00:20:44,890
Hey, reckless young man.

295
00:20:44,890 --> 00:20:51,690
You need to learn that some doors
in this world should never be opened.

296
00:20:53,662 --> 00:20:55,238
Surprise!

297
00:20:55,238 --> 00:20:57,466
Hi, my friend.

298
00:21:01,034 --> 00:21:02,833
I'll be offline for a bit.

299
00:21:03,602 --> 00:21:04,934
What are you doing here?

300
00:21:04,934 --> 00:21:07,558
Why are you...

301
00:21:07,558 --> 00:21:09,833
How did you know I was here?

302
00:21:17,626 --> 00:21:20,166
Still got those sticky fingers, I see.

303
00:21:21,318 --> 00:21:22,514
What's going on today?

304
00:21:22,514 --> 00:21:25,918
Why are you letting your guard down?
That's not like you.

305
00:21:25,918 --> 00:21:26,922
What brings you to Korea?

306
00:21:26,922 --> 00:21:29,133
I was bored, so I came to visit.

307
00:21:29,133 --> 00:21:31,866
Russia is too boring without you.

308
00:21:31,866 --> 00:21:33,999
Go. I'm working now.

309
00:21:35,694 --> 00:21:38,262
Well, is there a problem?

310
00:21:38,262 --> 00:21:41,466
The client has a visitor, so I'm standing by.

311
00:21:46,282 --> 00:21:48,566
Now that's more like you.

312
00:21:48,566 --> 00:21:52,218
But once the guest leaves, you can do it?

313
00:21:52,218 --> 00:21:53,709
You're still in the very early stages,

314
00:21:53,709 --> 00:21:56,633
so I think you were told to be extra careful.

315
00:21:58,790 --> 00:22:01,133
Where did you even...

316
00:22:01,818 --> 00:22:03,562
Isn't this the time

317
00:22:03,562 --> 00:22:06,766
when you should be focusing on
nothing but beautiful things?

318
00:22:08,182 --> 00:22:13,466
But if you absolutely have to do it,
how about hiring a mercenary?

319
00:22:19,638 --> 00:22:21,478
A mercenary?

320
00:22:21,478 --> 00:22:23,699
The best mercenary.

321
00:22:31,774 --> 00:22:35,166
Then you just pull the trigger.
I'll take care of the rest.

322
00:22:35,970 --> 00:22:37,930
Wise choice.

323
00:22:37,930 --> 00:22:40,738
Not yet, wait.

324
00:22:40,738 --> 00:22:43,499
I need to confirm the location first.

325
00:22:55,430 --> 00:22:58,299
Is there just one guest?

326
00:23:00,390 --> 00:23:02,090
Oh.

327
00:23:02,726 --> 00:23:04,426
A young boy?

328
00:23:04,426 --> 00:23:05,602
His son.

329
00:23:05,602 --> 00:23:09,199
Once the child has left, then...

330
00:23:09,199 --> 00:23:10,333
Target is down.

331
00:23:10,333 --> 00:23:12,399
What on earth are you doing?

332
00:23:19,366 --> 00:23:22,466
Calm down, Bo Na.

333
00:23:22,466 --> 00:23:25,762
You crazy punk! You want to die?

334
00:23:25,762 --> 00:23:30,633
The person holding the gun decides
when to pull the trigger.

335
00:23:30,633 --> 00:23:33,814
- You know that.
- The boy is innocent.

336
00:23:33,814 --> 00:23:35,342
He's done nothing wrong.

337
00:23:35,342 --> 00:23:41,190
"Your name, in death,
only ends up on your tombstone."

338
00:23:41,190 --> 00:23:47,450
"But your sins, even in death,
are passed down to your children."

339
00:23:47,450 --> 00:23:49,466
That's what Mama always used to say.

340
00:23:49,466 --> 00:23:51,199
Shut up!

341
00:23:59,618 --> 00:24:02,206
Did I kill a kid like someone else did?

342
00:24:02,206 --> 00:24:04,278
I didn't, right?

343
00:24:04,278 --> 00:24:05,810
So isn't that enough?

344
00:24:05,810 --> 00:24:09,006
Oh, calm down, Bo Na.

345
00:24:09,006 --> 00:24:11,999
The doctor said stress
isn't good for the baby...

346
00:24:44,599 --> 00:24:45,899
[Not Today, Kwon Tae Seong]

347
00:24:45,899 --> 00:24:48,333
Kwon Tae Seong?

348
00:24:49,462 --> 00:24:51,162
So he's a reporter?

349
00:24:52,734 --> 00:24:54,434
And what's this?

350
00:24:58,810 --> 00:25:00,766
Interesting.

351
00:25:28,554 --> 00:25:30,254
You're awake.

352
00:25:32,006 --> 00:25:34,378
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong.

353
00:25:34,378 --> 00:25:39,199
Forget everything that happened today.

354
00:25:39,942 --> 00:25:44,699
And from now on, you'd better
stop looking into Kingfisher.

355
00:25:46,930 --> 00:25:49,333
If you break your promise,

356
00:25:50,586 --> 00:25:54,126
your wife and your child,

357
00:25:54,126 --> 00:25:56,866
your family could be in danger.

358
00:26:02,754 --> 00:26:04,266
Calm down.

359
00:26:04,266 --> 00:26:07,298
Shh.

360
00:26:07,298 --> 00:26:11,833
As long as you keep your promise,
nothing will happen.

361
00:26:13,286 --> 00:26:15,566
Well, then...

362
00:26:21,198 --> 00:26:23,766
Goodnight, Tae Seong.

363
00:26:29,782 --> 00:26:33,486
Why are you still so angry, Yoo Bo Na?

364
00:26:33,486 --> 00:26:38,446
Did I put a blemish on
Kingfisher's flawless record?

365
00:26:38,446 --> 00:26:43,178
You left a scar on a child that
he'll never forget for the rest of his life.

366
00:26:43,178 --> 00:26:46,418
Did I force you to give up the gun?

367
00:26:46,418 --> 00:26:48,346
You were the one who chose.

368
00:26:48,346 --> 00:26:53,186
Don't you have to give something up
to protect something else?

369
00:26:53,186 --> 00:26:55,346
You're wrong.

370
00:26:55,346 --> 00:26:57,958
It wasn't a sacrifice. It was a mistake.

371
00:26:57,958 --> 00:27:00,082
My mistake was trusting you for a moment

372
00:27:00,082 --> 00:27:03,266
and forgetting what kind of punk you are.

373
00:27:04,158 --> 00:27:06,333
Leave while you're still alive.

374
00:27:07,878 --> 00:27:09,302
Aren't you going to ask this time?

375
00:27:09,302 --> 00:27:11,566
What brings me to Korea?

376
00:27:12,650 --> 00:27:14,938
Just stick to your word.

377
00:27:14,938 --> 00:27:16,799
This is your final warning.

378
00:27:21,358 --> 00:27:24,162
I'll stick to my word.

379
00:27:24,162 --> 00:27:27,699
Because you'll come
looking for me first anyway.

380
00:27:28,882 --> 00:27:30,966
And when that happens,

381
00:27:30,966 --> 00:27:34,999
what choice will you make then, Yoo Bo Na?

382
00:27:40,666 --> 00:27:42,666
[Caller ID Restricted:
You keep your promises well]

383
00:27:44,182 --> 00:27:46,414
[Good. Another good night, Tae Seong]
<i>Goodnight, Tae Seong.</i>

384
00:27:46,414 --> 00:27:49,133
Goodbye, Tae Seong.

385
00:28:05,366 --> 00:28:08,399
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

386
00:28:15,894 --> 00:28:19,766
Why'd you ask me to come to
such a secluded place?

387
00:28:26,166 --> 00:28:28,099
Are you Kingfisher?

388
00:28:30,099 --> 00:28:32,282
Are you seriously asking me that?

389
00:28:32,282 --> 00:28:34,099
The World Cup case and the Haegong-dong case.

390
00:28:34,099 --> 00:28:36,634
You were there for both major incidents.

391
00:28:36,634 --> 00:28:38,754
The odds of that are practically impossible.

392
00:28:38,754 --> 00:28:40,350
Are you still drunk?

393
00:28:40,350 --> 00:28:42,486
I'm a reporter, you punk!

394
00:28:42,486 --> 00:28:46,599
Tell me. Everything that happened that day.
I'm not joking.

395
00:28:51,194 --> 00:28:55,399
The seven-year-old boy
who was at the scene in Haegong-dong.

396
00:28:56,042 --> 00:28:58,286
What? Why are you bringing that up?

397
00:28:58,286 --> 00:28:59,499
If I didn't know about it,

398
00:28:59,499 --> 00:29:01,822
that means it was never opened up
to the press to protect that kid.

399
00:29:01,822 --> 00:29:03,414
Right, so?

400
00:29:03,414 --> 00:29:06,466
So I have an embargo too.

401
00:29:09,838 --> 00:29:11,538
What?

402
00:29:13,658 --> 00:29:16,299
I have someone I need to protect too.

403
00:29:21,299 --> 00:29:22,966
Let me ask you one thing.

404
00:29:22,966 --> 00:29:27,799
Are you sure the man you saw that day
was Kingfisher?

405
00:29:31,166 --> 00:29:32,454
What about you?

406
00:29:32,454 --> 00:29:36,233
Are you sure Kingfisher knew the son
was there and still pulled the trigger?

407
00:29:42,094 --> 00:29:46,166
I already heard it,
and I can't pretend I haven't.

408
00:29:46,166 --> 00:29:49,310
If that man really was Kingfisher,
then you're a witness.

409
00:29:49,310 --> 00:29:52,566
If not, you could be throwing
the investigation off course. Got it?

410
00:29:53,633 --> 00:29:54,633
I know.

411
00:29:54,633 --> 00:29:56,499
I can't wait long.

412
00:29:56,499 --> 00:29:58,157
Whatever the reason,
figure it out and tell me soon.

413
00:29:58,157 --> 00:30:00,466
Otherwise, I'll force the truth out of you.

414
00:30:01,698 --> 00:30:03,338
You know that, right?

415
00:30:03,338 --> 00:30:05,038
Oh, jeez.

416
00:30:15,166 --> 00:30:19,333
Your wife and your child,

417
00:30:20,038 --> 00:30:22,066
your family could be in danger.

418
00:30:22,066 --> 00:30:28,974
[Four Years Ago, The Night of "That Day"]

419
00:30:31,182 --> 00:30:32,966
Honey, what's wrong?

420
00:30:33,750 --> 00:30:36,754
You're barely eating. Is something wrong?

421
00:30:36,754 --> 00:30:38,946
No.

422
00:30:38,946 --> 00:30:40,646
Nothing's wrong.

423
00:30:42,138 --> 00:30:43,838
This is so good.

424
00:30:45,622 --> 00:30:48,762
By the way, didn't you say
you had something to show me?

425
00:30:48,762 --> 00:30:51,266
- Yeah.
- What is it?

426
00:30:55,450 --> 00:30:56,966
What is it?

427
00:30:56,966 --> 00:30:58,699
Look at this.

428
00:30:59,870 --> 00:31:01,599
What is it?

429
00:31:10,754 --> 00:31:14,166
I went to the hospital today, and I...

430
00:31:20,134 --> 00:31:21,834
<i>What a relief...</i>

431
00:31:22,586 --> 00:31:24,466
<i>to be able to come back.</i>

432
00:31:25,726 --> 00:31:27,426
Tae Seong.

433
00:31:29,602 --> 00:31:31,622
Are you crying?

434
00:31:31,622 --> 00:31:33,738
I'm not.

435
00:31:33,738 --> 00:31:36,014
<i>To come back to you, Bo Na,</i>

436
00:31:36,014 --> 00:31:39,318
<i>and to our baby.</i>

437
00:31:39,318 --> 00:31:41,166
<i>I'm just so relieved.</i>

438
00:31:41,934 --> 00:31:43,846
Are you crying again?

439
00:31:43,846 --> 00:31:44,846
Are you a crybaby?

440
00:31:44,846 --> 00:31:48,122
No, I'm not. I'm just happy. I'm happy.

441
00:31:48,122 --> 00:31:51,699
I'm not crying. Why are you crying?

442
00:32:01,814 --> 00:32:04,033
They said this is the gestational sac.

443
00:32:06,530 --> 00:32:08,306
Oh, my.

444
00:32:22,826 --> 00:32:25,966
Wow! It's orange.

445
00:32:25,966 --> 00:32:27,874
What color will it be?

446
00:32:27,874 --> 00:32:30,230
What's inside the orange?

447
00:32:30,230 --> 00:32:34,150
Ta-da! Wow, it's green.

448
00:32:34,150 --> 00:32:35,150
This is in here too...

449
00:32:35,150 --> 00:32:37,499
<i>Just as I thought,
those two are your Achilles' heels.</i>

450
00:32:37,499 --> 00:32:43,366
Having something to protect
is a fatal weakness for killers like us.

451
00:32:44,942 --> 00:32:47,199
It came out blue!

452
00:32:50,170 --> 00:32:51,730
- Mommy, why?
- Huh?

453
00:32:51,730 --> 00:32:52,950
Mommy, what's wrong?

454
00:32:52,950 --> 00:32:56,778
Mommy? I'm recharging my happiness.

455
00:32:56,778 --> 00:33:01,033
Holding Yul like this
fills Mommy's happiness battery.

456
00:33:01,033 --> 00:33:02,910
Me too! Happiness recharge!

457
00:33:02,910 --> 00:33:04,610
You too?

458
00:33:19,399 --> 00:33:22,366
[Durumi Electronics]

459
00:33:23,626 --> 00:33:25,638
Returned. It was useful.

460
00:33:25,638 --> 00:33:27,490
Just this? What about the others?

461
00:33:27,490 --> 00:33:29,674
I sent those somewhere.

462
00:33:29,674 --> 00:33:32,266
Don't charge it as an expense.
Just bill me for it.

463
00:33:42,630 --> 00:33:44,178
Gwangjang Market?

464
00:33:44,178 --> 00:33:45,933
I guess he was craving
some mung bean pancakes.

465
00:33:45,933 --> 00:33:47,626
So, that ugly mug is here?

466
00:33:47,626 --> 00:33:48,830
Tracking down restaurants?

467
00:33:48,830 --> 00:33:51,138
It doesn't look like he came
all this way just for a food tour.

468
00:33:51,138 --> 00:33:53,166
Please share this with me.

469
00:34:00,578 --> 00:34:03,279
Oh, that looks good.

470
00:34:03,279 --> 00:34:04,979
[Incoming Call]

471
00:34:07,090 --> 00:34:08,142
Not here.

472
00:34:08,142 --> 00:34:09,734
Looks like they got away.

473
00:34:09,734 --> 00:34:13,033
And Yoo Bo Na doesn't seem to know yet.

474
00:34:15,858 --> 00:34:17,574
Me?

475
00:34:17,574 --> 00:34:19,366
Well, since I'm here,

476
00:34:19,366 --> 00:34:22,499
maybe I'll check out some
good restaurants nearby.

477
00:34:22,499 --> 00:34:24,499
There are tons of great places
to eat in Korea.

478
00:34:27,950 --> 00:34:29,650
Mr. Kwon!

479
00:34:31,014 --> 00:34:32,818
Mr. Kwon!

480
00:34:32,818 --> 00:34:34,054
Yeah?

481
00:34:34,054 --> 00:34:38,299
What were you thinking about so deeply
that you didn't even hear me calling?

482
00:34:39,314 --> 00:34:42,462
Well, if you heard a voice again that
you first heard four years ago,

483
00:34:42,462 --> 00:34:44,562
do you think you'd recognize it?

484
00:34:44,562 --> 00:34:46,262
Huh?

485
00:34:47,622 --> 00:34:49,054
I'm not sure.

486
00:34:49,054 --> 00:34:54,462
Maybe if it's a familiar voice I hear
all the time, like a singer or actor,

487
00:34:55,298 --> 00:34:57,578
but just hearing it once? That's tough.

488
00:34:57,578 --> 00:34:59,999
Why do you ask?

489
00:35:00,666 --> 00:35:02,366
Never mind.

490
00:35:03,666 --> 00:35:05,874
Let's get to the meeting.

491
00:35:05,874 --> 00:35:10,294
Did you find out how many of
the parolees were violent offenders?

492
00:35:10,294 --> 00:35:13,218
I pulled the data from the past
ten years and analyzed it.

493
00:35:13,218 --> 00:35:16,006
[Number of Parolees by Violent Crime Type]
It's broken down by violent crime type,

494
00:35:16,006 --> 00:35:18,710
including murder, drugs, and sexual assault.

495
00:35:18,710 --> 00:35:22,966
And this is a separate list of
violent offenders released this year.

496
00:35:23,899 --> 00:35:26,599
You must've spent days on this.

497
00:35:27,833 --> 00:35:29,699
[2026 Violent Offenders Released on Parole]

498
00:35:30,633 --> 00:35:32,899
[Jang Eun Hak, Assault Resulting in Death]

499
00:35:35,386 --> 00:35:38,366
Mr. Kwon, what's wrong? Are you okay?

500
00:35:41,566 --> 00:35:44,266
[Model Prisoner]

501
00:35:58,374 --> 00:35:59,782
<i>What about you?</i>

502
00:35:59,782 --> 00:36:03,466
<i>Are you sure Kingfisher knew the son
was there and still pulled the trigger?</i>

503
00:36:08,010 --> 00:36:09,710
Mr. Lee!

504
00:36:10,386 --> 00:36:12,502
I got the victim statements
from the couple assault case.

505
00:36:12,502 --> 00:36:14,590
What should I do? Should I ask
the cybercrime unit for assistance?

506
00:36:14,590 --> 00:36:16,794
Yeah, go ahead.
And let me know if you find anything.

507
00:36:16,794 --> 00:36:18,494
Alright.

508
00:36:21,418 --> 00:36:23,799
What are you looking at so intently...

509
00:36:24,838 --> 00:36:26,250
The Haegong-dong Gosiwon?

510
00:36:26,250 --> 00:36:27,950
Why this case?

511
00:36:29,214 --> 00:36:30,242
Why aren't you asking me about it?

512
00:36:30,242 --> 00:36:32,182
About what?

513
00:36:32,182 --> 00:36:35,438
Oh, you mean the part about him
being killed in front of his son?

514
00:36:35,438 --> 00:36:37,110
That's just speculation, you know.

515
00:36:37,110 --> 00:36:40,044
Honestly, I don't think Kingfisher
would have pulled the trigger

516
00:36:40,044 --> 00:36:42,190
knowing there was a kid there.

517
00:36:42,190 --> 00:36:43,790
Well, look here.

518
00:36:43,790 --> 00:36:45,630
The windows in a Gosiwon
are pretty small, right?

519
00:36:45,630 --> 00:36:49,733
Couldn't there have been a blind spot
from the sniper's position?

520
00:36:54,582 --> 00:36:56,438
Beom.

521
00:36:56,438 --> 00:36:58,814
Leave work early today.

522
00:36:58,814 --> 00:37:00,514
Leave work?

523
00:37:01,118 --> 00:37:02,478
Are you telling me to go home?

524
00:37:02,478 --> 00:37:04,362
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]
You mean, not working late?

525
00:37:04,362 --> 00:37:06,966
Then do you want to work late?

526
00:37:06,966 --> 00:37:09,033
You're sure it's okay?

527
00:37:10,354 --> 00:37:11,354
Yay!

528
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:12,666
No taking it back, okay?

529
00:37:12,666 --> 00:37:16,099
Then I'll stop by the cybercrime unit
and head straight home.

530
00:37:17,842 --> 00:37:19,542
Sir, yes, sir!

531
00:37:20,610 --> 00:37:23,166
- Hey, where are you going?
- I'm going home! I'm off!

532
00:37:23,966 --> 00:37:25,866
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]

533
00:37:26,874 --> 00:37:29,066
Is the embargo over already?

534
00:37:30,286 --> 00:37:32,699
If you're calling me,
just say what's up. What is it?

535
00:37:32,699 --> 00:37:33,699
Dong Jin.

536
00:37:33,699 --> 00:37:37,354
Why are you calling me so sweetly?
You're making me nervous.

537
00:37:37,354 --> 00:37:39,333
<i>What's up? What's happening?</i>

538
00:37:40,454 --> 00:37:41,778
That punk's been released.

539
00:37:41,778 --> 00:37:44,906
That punk? Which punk?

540
00:37:44,906 --> 00:37:47,133
He was released on parole a month ago.

541
00:37:50,198 --> 00:37:51,898
What?

542
00:37:54,333 --> 00:37:58,778
<i>The so-called Gangmyeon-dong
Supermarket Murder Case.</i>

543
00:37:58,778 --> 00:38:00,674
[Client Information]
The perpetrator, Jang Eun Hak,

544
00:38:00,674 --> 00:38:02,518
brutally murdered a married couple

545
00:38:02,518 --> 00:38:05,418
who ran a neighborhood supermarket
with a broken soju bottle,

546
00:38:05,418 --> 00:38:07,890
fled the scene,
and was caught four years later.

547
00:38:07,890 --> 00:38:12,160
He was sentenced to 16 years in prison,
but he was paroled last month,

548
00:38:12,160 --> 00:38:14,599
just one year before his sentence
was due to end.

549
00:38:14,599 --> 00:38:15,846
[Dongwoon Furniture]
Hello.

550
00:38:15,846 --> 00:38:17,899
Oh, hello.

551
00:38:19,199 --> 00:38:20,539
- Are you looking for a bed?
- Yeah.

552
00:38:20,539 --> 00:38:23,133
What size bed are you looking for?

553
00:38:28,830 --> 00:38:30,818
Mr. Jang!

554
00:38:30,818 --> 00:38:32,086
Mr. Jang!

555
00:38:32,086 --> 00:38:35,070
- Oh, yeah.
- Move that.

556
00:38:35,070 --> 00:38:37,333
Oh, yes, understood.

557
00:38:38,982 --> 00:38:41,466
Oh, dear.

558
00:38:42,494 --> 00:38:46,570
Two people were brutally murdered,
and he only got 16 years?

559
00:38:46,570 --> 00:38:47,590
What?

560
00:38:47,590 --> 00:38:50,782
He was convicted of death resulting
from assault, not murder?

561
00:38:50,782 --> 00:38:51,810
That's right.

562
00:38:51,810 --> 00:38:53,414
He was 100 won short for soju,

563
00:38:53,414 --> 00:38:56,006
got into a scuffle,
and ended up committing murder.

564
00:38:56,006 --> 00:39:00,246
Then in court, he begged and pleaded,
claiming he was drunk and felt humiliated,

565
00:39:00,246 --> 00:39:03,462
so he did what he did.

566
00:39:03,462 --> 00:39:05,378
He exploited the leniency of the law.

567
00:39:05,378 --> 00:39:06,634
They say the law has mercy.

568
00:39:06,634 --> 00:39:10,770
Jeez, the victims' families
shed tears of blood.

569
00:39:10,770 --> 00:39:13,134
They do.

570
00:39:13,134 --> 00:39:15,099
Tears that never dry.

571
00:39:17,958 --> 00:39:22,799
But there's one notable detail there.

572
00:39:23,638 --> 00:39:27,874
<i>The victim's family has a son,</i>

573
00:39:27,874 --> 00:39:31,433
[Lee Dong Jin, 17 at the time]
and he's a detective.

574
00:39:32,486 --> 00:39:35,774
What's even more interesting is that

575
00:39:35,774 --> 00:39:38,333
he was once assigned to a Kingfisher case.

576
00:39:39,678 --> 00:39:42,139
Wow, what an irony.

577
00:39:42,139 --> 00:39:46,038
A police officer whose family was
victimized by a crime, chasing Kingfisher.

578
00:39:46,038 --> 00:39:48,662
With such a light sentence,
he must be devastated to find out

579
00:39:48,662 --> 00:39:50,118
the guy even got parole.

580
00:39:50,118 --> 00:39:52,533
Not devastated. Furious.

581
00:39:53,531 --> 00:39:55,786
Do you think he might do something dangerous?

582
00:39:55,786 --> 00:39:56,826
I know.

583
00:39:56,826 --> 00:40:00,133
He's a cop, and he has a gun.

584
00:40:00,814 --> 00:40:03,133
No. He's not that kind of person.

585
00:40:03,810 --> 00:40:07,462
If he wanted personal revenge,
he wouldn't have become a cop.

586
00:40:07,462 --> 00:40:10,650
He believes in making criminals pay
within the law.

587
00:40:10,650 --> 00:40:12,466
That's what the police are there for.

588
00:40:24,033 --> 00:40:27,133
[Seoul Nambu Police Station, Lee Dong Jin]

589
00:40:31,934 --> 00:40:33,578
Se Ah.

590
00:40:33,578 --> 00:40:34,678
A date?

591
00:40:34,678 --> 00:40:36,633
Just the two of us?

592
00:40:37,590 --> 00:40:40,114
Really? Then where should we meet?

593
00:40:40,114 --> 00:40:42,090
Meeting one-on-one outside...

594
00:40:42,090 --> 00:40:44,858
Classic sister-in-law move,
summoning her brother's wife like this.

595
00:40:44,858 --> 00:40:47,890
Still, isn't a sister-in-law easier
to deal with than a mother-in-law?

596
00:40:47,890 --> 00:40:51,149
There's a reason they say
a meddling sister-in-law is even worse.

597
00:40:51,149 --> 00:40:55,299
She's in trouble, or she's about to be.

598
00:41:07,818 --> 00:41:09,970
If you find anything,
please let me know right away.

599
00:41:09,970 --> 00:41:11,670
Sir, yes, sir!

600
00:41:18,362 --> 00:41:21,466
<i>I'm leaving work on time
for the first time in a million years.</i>

601
00:41:21,466 --> 00:41:23,002
Want to hit the arcade?

602
00:41:23,002 --> 00:41:24,850
<i>Nope. I've got a date.</i>

603
00:41:24,850 --> 00:41:26,550
A date?

604
00:41:27,964 --> 00:41:29,045
With a guy?

605
00:41:29,045 --> 00:41:30,745
<i>With my sister-in-law.</i>

606
00:41:31,370 --> 00:41:33,399
Figures.

607
00:41:36,190 --> 00:41:38,782
Then what should I do?

608
00:41:38,782 --> 00:41:39,894
Bo Na, over here.

609
00:41:39,894 --> 00:41:42,226
They say this place is seriously good.

610
00:41:42,226 --> 00:41:44,270
- Wow!
- Looks like there's no line today.

611
00:41:44,270 --> 00:41:46,113
- Welcome.
- Table for two.

612
00:41:46,113 --> 00:41:47,759
- Do you have a reservation?
- No.

613
00:41:47,759 --> 00:41:50,602
You have to book through
our app before you come.

614
00:41:50,602 --> 00:41:52,758
- Through an app?
- Yeah, I'm sorry.

615
00:41:52,758 --> 00:41:55,094
Then would you like to wait?

616
00:41:55,094 --> 00:41:56,794
[Waitlist]
Wait...

617
00:41:57,418 --> 00:41:58,446
There are like 20 people waiting.

618
00:41:58,446 --> 00:41:59,966
- What do we do?
- Number 35!

619
00:41:59,966 --> 00:42:02,066
- Yes.
- This way, please.

620
00:42:03,370 --> 00:42:04,602
Thank you.

621
00:42:04,602 --> 00:42:05,633
Enjoy your food.

622
00:42:05,633 --> 00:42:06,833
Start with this, like this.

623
00:42:06,833 --> 00:42:08,433
Oh, Bo Na, wait.

624
00:42:08,433 --> 00:42:10,433
No? Right now...

625
00:42:16,250 --> 00:42:18,999
Bo Na, should we take a picture together?

626
00:42:21,133 --> 00:42:22,333
<i>Don't look at the camera.</i>

627
00:42:22,333 --> 00:42:23,966
<i>Yes, pretend you're not
looking and act casual.</i>

628
00:42:23,966 --> 00:42:25,354
Try to look as pretty as possible.

629
00:42:25,354 --> 00:42:27,890
Two? Give me a pretty pose!

630
00:42:27,890 --> 00:42:29,199
- That's so cute.
- Ta-da!

631
00:42:29,199 --> 00:42:30,388
How is it?

632
00:42:30,388 --> 00:42:31,699
Oh, my, you look like a bunny!

633
00:42:31,699 --> 00:42:33,899
- How do you do this? A heart.
- A heart.

634
00:42:38,726 --> 00:42:41,926
Mom, you're really something else, huh?

635
00:42:41,926 --> 00:42:45,978
You badmouth Bo Na,
but you still make her all those side dishes.

636
00:42:45,978 --> 00:42:48,794
Oh, please. What are you talking about?

637
00:42:48,794 --> 00:42:50,618
Am I doing it for her?

638
00:42:50,618 --> 00:42:53,618
I make it to feed my own son.

639
00:42:53,618 --> 00:42:57,333
Oh, dear. Other mothers-in-law
pack all kinds of food

640
00:42:57,333 --> 00:42:59,114
for their sons-in-law.

641
00:42:59,114 --> 00:43:01,098
Jeez, there you go again.

642
00:43:01,098 --> 00:43:03,302
- I'm exhausted.
- Oh, you're here?

643
00:43:03,302 --> 00:43:05,006
Sun Il, please get me a glass of water.

644
00:43:05,006 --> 00:43:06,618
Alright.

645
00:43:06,618 --> 00:43:07,794
Where did you go?

646
00:43:07,794 --> 00:43:09,782
Oh, the department store.

647
00:43:09,782 --> 00:43:13,250
You know we're meeting Jun Woo's
future in-laws the day after tomorrow.

648
00:43:13,250 --> 00:43:16,199
Oh, right. Your second son's
wedding date is set.

649
00:43:16,199 --> 00:43:17,199
But why the department store?

650
00:43:17,199 --> 00:43:19,970
Well, I need something decent to wear.

651
00:43:19,970 --> 00:43:23,282
Seon Ja, what did you wear for
Tae Seong's family meeting?

652
00:43:23,282 --> 00:43:24,834
What?

653
00:43:24,834 --> 00:43:27,074
Well, just something simple.

654
00:43:27,074 --> 00:43:29,718
Oh, right. You never had one, did you?

655
00:43:29,718 --> 00:43:32,714
Oh, lucky you. You had it easy.

656
00:43:32,714 --> 00:43:34,162
Oh, my back.

657
00:43:34,162 --> 00:43:35,758
What do you mean I didn't have one?

658
00:43:35,758 --> 00:43:38,910
I did it twice for Sun Il and Du Ri.

659
00:43:38,910 --> 00:43:43,066
Is meeting your daughter's in-laws
the same as meeting your son's?

660
00:43:44,374 --> 00:43:47,433
They're basically the same.

661
00:43:48,633 --> 00:43:52,578
You can tell what kind of family
you're dealing with by meeting the parents.

662
00:43:52,578 --> 00:43:55,994
Both of our future in-laws are educators.

663
00:43:55,994 --> 00:43:59,874
Maybe that's why their daughter
is so well-mannered,

664
00:43:59,874 --> 00:44:02,526
and her face is so bright, without a shadow.

665
00:44:02,526 --> 00:44:06,233
You can just tell
she grew up surrounded by love.

666
00:44:07,134 --> 00:44:11,070
Oh, dear. Is it a little awkward
saying this in front of you?

667
00:44:11,070 --> 00:44:12,399
- Your daughter-in-law...
- You punk!

668
00:44:12,399 --> 00:44:13,766
- Shut your mouth!
- Oh, my.

669
00:44:13,766 --> 00:44:14,933
Oh, my, what's gotten into you?

670
00:44:14,933 --> 00:44:16,630
Oh, my. What did I even do?

671
00:44:16,630 --> 00:44:20,370
Fine. I never had a formal family meeting,
and I don't have any in-laws.

672
00:44:20,370 --> 00:44:22,133
Because my daughter-in-law is an orphan.

673
00:44:22,133 --> 00:44:24,062
So what? What about it?

674
00:44:24,062 --> 00:44:25,894
Did you contribute anything?

675
00:44:25,894 --> 00:44:28,674
Well, I gave quite a lot
for the wedding gift.

676
00:44:28,674 --> 00:44:31,938
Why are you making such a fuss over
getting an orphaned daughter-in-law?

677
00:44:31,938 --> 00:44:34,526
Wow, I've been friends
with you all my life...

678
00:44:34,526 --> 00:44:36,414
You little punk. I'm going to get you today.

679
00:44:36,414 --> 00:44:37,666
Oh, my. Oh, my!

680
00:44:37,666 --> 00:44:39,566
- Mom!
- What's gotten into you?

681
00:44:42,510 --> 00:44:44,210
Wow!

682
00:44:47,666 --> 00:44:51,218
Se Ah, what do you usually do
when you hang out with your friends?

683
00:44:51,218 --> 00:44:52,458
Me?

684
00:44:52,458 --> 00:44:56,933
We'd go for chicken feet and soju.
Or cold pork belly and beer.

685
00:44:58,918 --> 00:45:00,666
Was it that obvious?

686
00:45:02,233 --> 00:45:05,747
Actually, I did some research before I came.

687
00:45:05,747 --> 00:45:08,899
I was wondering what young people
do for fun these days.

688
00:45:08,899 --> 00:45:11,433
Like the place we went to earlier.

689
00:45:11,433 --> 00:45:16,433
It's not really my thing,
but I thought you might enjoy it.

690
00:45:17,362 --> 00:45:19,833
So it was your first time.

691
00:45:22,599 --> 00:45:27,833
I actually love just sitting around
doing nothing with you.

692
00:45:28,899 --> 00:45:29,974
Really?

693
00:45:29,974 --> 00:45:31,733
Yeah.

694
00:45:34,374 --> 00:45:37,626
Then where do you actually go most often?

695
00:45:37,626 --> 00:45:39,305
Let's have that be our last stop.

696
00:45:39,305 --> 00:45:41,005
Is that what you want?

697
00:45:42,250 --> 00:45:45,066
There's one place.

698
00:45:48,066 --> 00:45:50,133
[Se Dol, You Have a New Message]

699
00:45:54,482 --> 00:45:57,099
<i>Get to the PC bang now.</i>

700
00:46:03,474 --> 00:46:05,066
Hey, why are you so late?

701
00:46:05,066 --> 00:46:06,499
You said you were leaving work on time.

702
00:46:06,499 --> 00:46:08,230
Huh?

703
00:46:08,230 --> 00:46:12,662
I went somewhere else first.
What, you think you're my only friend?

704
00:46:12,662 --> 00:46:14,733
Hey, say hi. This is my sister-in-law.

705
00:46:14,733 --> 00:46:16,622
Bo Na, this is my friend, Mr. Tiger.

706
00:46:16,622 --> 00:46:18,599
- Hello.
- Oh, hi.

707
00:46:18,599 --> 00:46:20,299
I didn't know your friend was a guy.

708
00:46:20,299 --> 00:46:21,466
Is he your boyfriend?

709
00:46:21,466 --> 00:46:23,639
No, we're just friends.

710
00:46:23,639 --> 00:46:25,730
Nice to meet you properly.

711
00:46:25,730 --> 00:46:27,230
I'm Beom Seong Hun.

712
00:46:27,230 --> 00:46:29,433
I'm really sorry
I couldn't make it to the wedding.

713
00:46:29,433 --> 00:46:32,222
Oh, don't be.

714
00:46:32,222 --> 00:46:34,599
- He's handsome.
- What?

715
00:46:35,654 --> 00:46:38,099
Then, let's skip the formalities
and sit down.

716
00:46:38,099 --> 00:46:40,738
Alright, your only mission today is

717
00:46:40,738 --> 00:46:45,115
to show my sister-in-law
the true taste of victory. Got it?

718
00:46:45,115 --> 00:46:47,533
Well, that's a lot of weight on my shoulders.

719
00:46:47,533 --> 00:46:49,433
I'm counting on you.

720
00:46:50,438 --> 00:46:53,842
Bo Na, since my friend's here,
want to try an FPS game?

721
00:46:53,842 --> 00:46:55,078
FPS?

722
00:46:55,078 --> 00:46:59,554
When you're stressed,
nothing beats shooting things.

723
00:46:59,554 --> 00:47:01,202
Bang, bang!

724
00:47:01,202 --> 00:47:03,134
Sniping.

725
00:47:03,134 --> 00:47:05,326
There's a game where you snipe people?

726
00:47:05,326 --> 00:47:08,733
Yeah, it's a little difficult.

727
00:47:08,733 --> 00:47:11,133
But you can just stick with us,
and you'll be fine.

728
00:47:11,133 --> 00:47:14,854
He'll do all the killing anyway.

729
00:47:14,854 --> 00:47:15,966
Please take care of me.

730
00:47:15,966 --> 00:47:16,966
Oh, come on.

731
00:47:16,966 --> 00:47:19,499
I'm not that good.

732
00:47:19,499 --> 00:47:21,566
Okay, shall we give it a try?

733
00:47:21,566 --> 00:47:23,266
Sure.

734
00:47:26,034 --> 00:47:28,842
There, there's someone over there.
SW 1 direction.

735
00:47:28,842 --> 00:47:30,174
Oh, okay, got it.

736
00:47:30,174 --> 00:47:32,114
Oh, nice.

737
00:47:32,114 --> 00:47:33,422
Well, it's nothing.

738
00:47:33,422 --> 00:47:34,686
Watch out, there's one more.

739
00:47:34,686 --> 00:47:37,414
Hey, behind that wall. See him?

740
00:47:37,414 --> 00:47:39,118
Wow, what's gotten into you?

741
00:47:39,118 --> 00:47:40,133
Hey, ping one, ping one.

742
00:47:40,133 --> 00:47:42,399
Oh, yeah! Assist!

743
00:47:42,399 --> 00:47:44,399
Oh, your aim is really good today.

744
00:47:44,399 --> 00:47:46,299
What's with the sudden praise?

745
00:47:48,022 --> 00:47:50,799
Oh, why are you so good today?

746
00:47:50,799 --> 00:47:51,926
I'll take care of him.

747
00:47:51,926 --> 00:47:54,366
- One team left, one team.
- Okay.

748
00:47:54,366 --> 00:47:57,766
I smell chicken.

749
00:47:57,766 --> 00:47:58,866
What is it?

750
00:47:58,866 --> 00:48:00,466
This feels like a chicken dinner.

751
00:48:00,466 --> 00:48:03,233
[Match in progress in the marked zone.
45 seconds left]

752
00:48:03,233 --> 00:48:04,966
Chicken!

753
00:48:06,299 --> 00:48:07,866
Bo Na, how was it? Winning's fun, right?

754
00:48:07,866 --> 00:48:10,433
It's so much fun.

755
00:48:11,399 --> 00:48:12,462
This is really fun.

756
00:48:12,462 --> 00:48:13,738
- Right?
- Yeah.

757
00:48:13,738 --> 00:48:18,858
Hey, thanks to you,
my years of pent-up stress are gone!

758
00:48:18,858 --> 00:48:20,462
You were great.

759
00:48:20,462 --> 00:48:21,730
No, it wasn't me.

760
00:48:21,730 --> 00:48:23,430
What do you mean?

761
00:48:25,342 --> 00:48:26,654
[We Won! Chicken for Dinner Tonight!]
What?

762
00:48:26,654 --> 00:48:28,310
Three kills?

763
00:48:28,310 --> 00:48:29,790
You only got three kills?

764
00:48:29,790 --> 00:48:31,718
Then, how did we even win?

765
00:48:31,718 --> 00:48:33,550
Come with me.

766
00:48:33,550 --> 00:48:35,630
[Team Rank 1, 15 Kills]
Huh?

767
00:48:35,630 --> 00:48:38,126
Bo Na, what is this?

768
00:48:38,126 --> 00:48:39,318
What?

769
00:48:39,318 --> 00:48:41,870
You got all those kills!

770
00:48:41,870 --> 00:48:43,130
This isn't your first time, is it?

771
00:48:43,130 --> 00:48:45,578
I think we just discovered
your hidden talent.

772
00:48:45,578 --> 00:48:49,233
Were you a sniper in a past life?

773
00:48:49,233 --> 00:48:50,233
Maybe I was.

774
00:48:50,233 --> 00:48:53,534
- This is amazing!
- I guess I got lucky today.

775
00:48:53,534 --> 00:48:55,782
Well, let's play one more round.

776
00:48:55,782 --> 00:48:57,099
- You want to?
- Yeah.

777
00:48:57,099 --> 00:48:58,466
Alright.

778
00:48:58,466 --> 00:49:00,433
This game isn't exactly easy.

779
00:49:00,433 --> 00:49:03,133
[13 Kills, 14 Kills, 16 Kills]

780
00:49:04,477 --> 00:49:06,177
[17 Kills]

781
00:49:14,625 --> 00:49:16,325
Oh, dear.

782
00:49:20,299 --> 00:49:22,550
[Team Rank 1, 19 Kills]

783
00:49:22,550 --> 00:49:23,778
Wow...

784
00:49:23,778 --> 00:49:25,466
No way...

785
00:49:25,466 --> 00:49:28,033
This isn't possible.

786
00:49:29,458 --> 00:49:34,133
Se Ah must've been enjoying herself
to keep you out that late.

787
00:49:34,133 --> 00:49:36,433
I had so much fun.

788
00:49:36,433 --> 00:49:39,334
I got to try a lot of things
I'd never done before. It was really fun.

789
00:49:39,334 --> 00:49:42,134
<i>Looks like Se Ah really did
something big today.</i>

790
00:49:42,134 --> 00:49:45,099
It's okay. Take your time.

791
00:49:45,099 --> 00:49:47,666
<i>I'm going to take Yul to the store later.</i>

792
00:49:47,666 --> 00:49:49,002
Sun Il said to bring over some fresh kimchi.

793
00:49:49,002 --> 00:49:51,154
Really? I love your mom's fresh kimchi.

794
00:49:51,154 --> 00:49:52,534
Please bring lots.

795
00:49:52,534 --> 00:49:57,434
Today I discovered a side of my sister-in-law
that completely blew me away.

796
00:49:57,434 --> 00:49:58,902
Isn't she seriously cool?

797
00:49:58,902 --> 00:50:01,606
How old is your brother's kid again?

798
00:50:01,606 --> 00:50:04,430
Yul? Four? Why do you ask that?

799
00:50:04,430 --> 00:50:07,266
Then the timing lines up perfectly, huh?

800
00:50:08,278 --> 00:50:09,633
You know I have a good gut feeling, right?

801
00:50:09,633 --> 00:50:11,954
What, you?

802
00:50:11,954 --> 00:50:14,099
I think your sister-in-law...

803
00:50:16,430 --> 00:50:18,754
might be hiding her true identity.

804
00:50:18,754 --> 00:50:20,746
What identity?

805
00:50:20,746 --> 00:50:24,266
The legend who vanished without a trace
in the spring four years ago...

806
00:50:26,594 --> 00:50:28,242
the legend of FPS games!

807
00:50:28,242 --> 00:50:30,633
But she was on maternity leave.

808
00:50:30,633 --> 00:50:34,534
A gaming genius who shows up
every few years and sweeps the top records?

809
00:50:34,534 --> 00:50:36,133
Enough with the nonsense!

810
00:50:36,133 --> 00:50:38,218
Okay.

811
00:50:38,218 --> 00:50:39,918
Well...

812
00:50:42,282 --> 00:50:46,766
Bo Na, were you surprised
when I suddenly asked you out today?

813
00:50:46,766 --> 00:50:50,662
No. I was just... excited.

814
00:50:50,662 --> 00:50:54,522
It's been so long since I've gone out
and had fun without Yul. It was exciting.

815
00:50:54,522 --> 00:50:56,054
Really?

816
00:50:56,054 --> 00:51:00,286
So you haven't really seen
your friends since you had Yul?

817
00:51:00,286 --> 00:51:03,206
I guess I don't really have many friends.

818
00:51:03,206 --> 00:51:04,599
I'm not sure why.

819
00:51:04,599 --> 00:51:07,170
Oh, I see.

820
00:51:07,170 --> 00:51:11,678
I feel like I got a little
closer to you today.

821
00:51:11,678 --> 00:51:13,570
You do?

822
00:51:13,570 --> 00:51:18,014
Actually, there was something
I wanted to ask you.

823
00:51:18,014 --> 00:51:21,342
That's partly why I asked you out.

824
00:51:21,342 --> 00:51:23,654
But I've changed my mind.

825
00:51:23,654 --> 00:51:25,798
I'm going to ask you for something else!

826
00:51:25,798 --> 00:51:27,010
What is it?

827
00:51:27,010 --> 00:51:31,822
From now on, please speak casually with me.

828
00:51:31,822 --> 00:51:36,566
I'm Tae Seong's younger sister,
and we're family.

829
00:51:38,230 --> 00:51:40,018
Okay, should we do that then?

830
00:51:40,018 --> 00:51:41,562
Really? Oh, yeah!

831
00:51:41,562 --> 00:51:43,054
What a rewarding day!

832
00:51:43,054 --> 00:51:46,066
Then can I link arms with you?

833
00:51:46,066 --> 00:51:47,230
Sure, come here.

834
00:51:47,230 --> 00:51:49,233
Oh, really?

835
00:51:51,846 --> 00:51:53,699
This is nice!

836
00:51:53,699 --> 00:51:55,499
[Tae Seong Chicken]

837
00:51:55,499 --> 00:51:58,826
Mom, are you still mad?

838
00:51:58,826 --> 00:52:00,362
You really hold a grudge.

839
00:52:00,362 --> 00:52:03,699
Come on, it's not like her saying
rude things is anything new.

840
00:52:03,699 --> 00:52:06,654
Still, you don't like it when others
badmouth your daughter-in-law, do you?

841
00:52:06,654 --> 00:52:09,184
Of course I don't, huh?

842
00:52:09,184 --> 00:52:10,702
She's my daughter now too.

843
00:52:10,702 --> 00:52:13,858
If anyone's going to criticize her,
it should be me. Who is she?

844
00:52:13,858 --> 00:52:16,818
What, "bright"?

845
00:52:16,818 --> 00:52:18,642
Is that supposed to mean
my girl is dark and dull?

846
00:52:18,642 --> 00:52:20,533
Oh, my. "My girl"?

847
00:52:20,533 --> 00:52:22,058
That darn punk.

848
00:52:22,058 --> 00:52:23,994
Who's bragging?

849
00:52:23,994 --> 00:52:26,113
I hated the orphan daughter-in-law too,

850
00:52:26,113 --> 00:52:28,690
and I was annoyed about
not having a meeting with her family.

851
00:52:28,690 --> 00:52:31,690
- Mom!
- What mom in this world

852
00:52:31,690 --> 00:52:34,833
wants to give her precious son to an orphan?

853
00:52:34,833 --> 00:52:36,278
But as time went by...

854
00:52:36,278 --> 00:52:38,099
Mom!

855
00:52:50,114 --> 00:52:52,261
Oh, you're here?

856
00:52:52,261 --> 00:52:53,961
Yes, Mother.

857
00:52:55,402 --> 00:52:58,233
Wait, how are you two together again...

858
00:53:01,257 --> 00:53:03,133
Honey, take Yul outside first.

859
00:53:03,133 --> 00:53:04,133
Huh?

860
00:53:04,133 --> 00:53:06,566
Please. Just go. I'm asking you.

861
00:53:08,062 --> 00:53:09,466
[Red Bean Bread]
Mother, have this when you get hungry.

862
00:53:09,466 --> 00:53:10,474
It's your favorite red bean bread.

863
00:53:10,474 --> 00:53:13,499
Oh, okay. Thank you.

864
00:53:23,233 --> 00:53:25,399
[Red Bean Bread]

865
00:53:27,466 --> 00:53:31,399
You should've told me
you were bringing her with you.

866
00:53:32,630 --> 00:53:34,966
Did you eat dinner?

867
00:53:37,050 --> 00:53:39,262
Mom.

868
00:53:39,262 --> 00:53:41,233
Apologize to Yul's mom.

869
00:53:41,233 --> 00:53:46,042
Well, I didn't say it for her to hear.

870
00:53:46,042 --> 00:53:48,133
But she heard you.

871
00:53:49,750 --> 00:53:52,878
Did I make anything up?

872
00:53:52,878 --> 00:53:55,310
She is an orphan.

873
00:53:55,310 --> 00:53:57,154
Mom!

874
00:53:57,154 --> 00:54:00,274
Just because she's an orphan doesn't mean
you can treat her however you want.

875
00:54:00,274 --> 00:54:02,966
What did I do...

876
00:54:05,848 --> 00:54:09,520
So what? What if I say I can't apologize?

877
00:54:09,520 --> 00:54:12,299
What? Are you going to stop seeing me?

878
00:54:25,978 --> 00:54:30,129
Jeez, they say raising kids is useless.

879
00:54:30,129 --> 00:54:33,578
All you care about is
how precious your wife is.

880
00:54:33,578 --> 00:54:35,278
Mom.

881
00:54:35,966 --> 00:54:37,442
Mom, honestly, you're sorry, aren't you?

882
00:54:37,442 --> 00:54:39,642
Sorry for what?

883
00:54:39,642 --> 00:54:43,033
People even talk bad about the president
in private. What's the big deal?

884
00:54:44,430 --> 00:54:48,233
Why did they have to walk in
at that exact moment and make such a fuss?

885
00:54:49,934 --> 00:54:52,999
What lousy timing.

886
00:54:59,202 --> 00:55:00,490
I'm sorry.

887
00:55:00,490 --> 00:55:02,766
I'll apologize on her behalf.

888
00:55:04,394 --> 00:55:07,474
Me? I'm fine.

889
00:55:07,474 --> 00:55:09,566
It doesn't bother me.

890
00:55:12,538 --> 00:55:14,799
She's your mom.

891
00:55:14,799 --> 00:55:16,233
Maybe it's because I'm a mom too?

892
00:55:16,233 --> 00:55:19,899
I think I understand a little.

893
00:55:20,911 --> 00:55:23,733
That feeling of being helpless
in front of your child.

894
00:55:24,382 --> 00:55:27,999
That instinct to put your child first.

895
00:55:33,010 --> 00:55:37,133
Being a mom doesn't excuse everything.
She was still wrong.

896
00:55:40,802 --> 00:55:44,138
Then should I tell you exactly what I think?

897
00:55:44,138 --> 00:55:46,499
Isn't your mom being a little too much?

898
00:55:47,833 --> 00:55:51,214
Well, I'm not the person I used to be.

899
00:55:51,214 --> 00:55:52,618
I'm not alone anymore.

900
00:55:52,618 --> 00:55:54,633
I have a husband and a daughter.

901
00:55:54,633 --> 00:55:58,070
I have a mother-in-law
and three sisters-in-law.

902
00:55:58,070 --> 00:56:01,399
What matters is the present,
not the past. Isn't it?

903
00:56:05,506 --> 00:56:07,206
But...

904
00:56:08,366 --> 00:56:11,399
I believe she'll understand someday.

905
00:56:11,399 --> 00:56:14,033
If we keep arguing and making up like this...

906
00:56:15,533 --> 00:56:17,766
Look at you, saying things like that.

907
00:56:18,466 --> 00:56:22,222
I mean, we laugh and cry together,

908
00:56:22,222 --> 00:56:26,754
get on each other's nerves,
hurt each other...

909
00:56:26,754 --> 00:56:28,899
Isn't that what family is?

910
00:56:29,678 --> 00:56:32,999
So we're really going at it.

911
00:56:34,374 --> 00:56:36,633
Going at it? What are we going at?

912
00:56:37,434 --> 00:56:39,417
What do you want to eat, Yul?

913
00:56:39,417 --> 00:56:41,362
Should we stir-fry Yul's favorite sausages?

914
00:56:41,362 --> 00:56:43,466
Yeah, I like sausages.

915
00:56:43,466 --> 00:56:44,833
Let's go stir-fry some sausages.

916
00:56:44,833 --> 00:56:47,533
Let's go make some sausages!

917
00:57:13,830 --> 00:57:16,166
Why are the lights off?

918
00:57:16,166 --> 00:57:18,033
Are they closed already?

919
00:57:21,433 --> 00:57:24,899
The door isn't even locked. What's going on?

920
00:57:49,878 --> 00:57:51,699
Mom.

921
00:57:51,699 --> 00:57:53,399
Mom.

922
00:57:54,099 --> 00:57:55,833
Dad.

923
00:58:16,733 --> 00:58:19,899
[Dongwoon Furniture]

924
00:58:19,899 --> 00:58:21,726
Twenty percent off for a set.

925
00:58:21,726 --> 00:58:24,438
Welcome. Can I help you find anything?

926
00:58:24,438 --> 00:58:25,966
I'm just looking around.

927
00:58:25,966 --> 00:58:27,933
Sure. Take your time.

928
00:58:28,733 --> 00:58:31,353
Just write your address here.

929
00:58:31,353 --> 00:58:34,633
We'll have it delivered by truck tomorrow.

930
00:58:34,633 --> 00:58:37,633
[Dongwoon Furniture, We Sell the Cheapest]

931
00:58:38,730 --> 00:58:40,433
I'm back.

932
00:58:45,234 --> 00:58:48,782
You left for that delivery ages ago.
Why are you only getting back now?

933
00:58:48,782 --> 00:58:50,698
Were you goofing off somewhere again?

934
00:58:50,698 --> 00:58:55,592
No. I took a wrong turn
on the way. I'm sorry.

935
00:58:55,592 --> 00:58:58,250
And what about the chair
delivered to Taeheung-dong this morning?

936
00:58:58,250 --> 00:59:02,784
What did you do this time?
We got a complaint saying one leg is wobbly.

937
00:59:02,784 --> 00:59:04,034
What?

938
00:59:04,034 --> 00:59:06,433
Well... that can't be right.

939
00:59:06,433 --> 00:59:10,442
How many times have I told you to be careful
when carrying things up and down?

940
00:59:10,442 --> 00:59:14,030
Why do you keep making us
go back for repairs? Oh, my.

941
00:59:14,030 --> 00:59:16,966
How am I supposed to keep you on like this?

942
00:59:16,966 --> 00:59:19,066
I'm sorry. I'll make sure
it doesn't happen again.

943
00:59:19,066 --> 00:59:21,718
Forget it! Go back to work.

944
00:59:21,718 --> 00:59:23,290
Jeez.

945
00:59:23,290 --> 00:59:25,066
I'm sorry.

946
00:59:25,715 --> 00:59:29,333
Jeez, that punk is really
on my case. Darn it.

947
00:59:36,299 --> 00:59:38,666
[Dongwoon Furniture]

948
00:59:51,402 --> 00:59:53,333
Darn it.

949
01:01:06,305 --> 01:01:08,805
Darn it! Seriously!

950
01:01:27,650 --> 01:01:29,350
Hey!

951
01:01:31,677 --> 01:01:33,377
You punk!

952
01:01:34,594 --> 01:01:36,299
Honey!

953
01:01:38,402 --> 01:01:42,154
So why did you keep ignoring me? Why?

954
01:01:42,154 --> 01:01:44,366
Why?

955
01:01:44,366 --> 01:01:46,066
You punk!

956
01:01:48,846 --> 01:01:51,933
Police! Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak!

957
01:01:57,690 --> 01:01:58,966
Shoot me.

958
01:01:58,966 --> 01:02:01,664
Go ahead. Shoot me, you punk!

959
01:02:01,664 --> 01:02:04,666
If you want to see her die right here...

960
01:02:04,666 --> 01:02:08,866
Please help me...

961
01:02:12,666 --> 01:02:14,850
Last warning.

962
01:02:14,850 --> 01:02:16,198
Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak.

963
01:02:16,198 --> 01:02:19,880
Who on earth are you to tell me
what to do, you punk?

964
01:02:19,880 --> 01:02:21,882
I'll decide what to do
with my own knife, you punk!

965
01:02:21,882 --> 01:02:22,890
Jang Eun Hak!

966
01:02:22,890 --> 01:02:26,426
Please help me.

967
01:02:26,426 --> 01:02:27,666
Help me.

968
01:02:27,666 --> 01:02:31,350
Please help me.

969
01:02:31,350 --> 01:02:33,338
Let the woman go.

970
01:02:33,338 --> 01:02:38,543
I'm going to kill every punk
who looks down on me!

971
01:02:38,543 --> 01:02:40,266
You little punks, huh?

972
01:02:40,266 --> 01:02:41,933
Hey, you looked down on me too, didn't you?

973
01:02:41,933 --> 01:02:43,633
You little...

974
01:02:50,433 --> 01:02:51,433
Drop the knife, Jang Eun Hak!

975
01:02:51,433 --> 01:02:53,566
Honey, honey!

976
01:03:00,266 --> 01:03:01,999
Jang Eun Hak!

977
01:03:04,798 --> 01:03:07,066
Apply pressure to stop the bleeding
and call an ambulance.

978
01:03:07,066 --> 01:03:08,766
Hurry!

979
01:03:20,322 --> 01:03:22,022
Hey!

980
01:03:36,278 --> 01:03:38,399
You punk, stop right there!

981
01:03:43,318 --> 01:03:45,033
Jang Eun Hak!

982
01:03:50,946 --> 01:03:52,646
Hey!

983
01:03:55,350 --> 01:03:57,050
Stop!

984
01:03:58,674 --> 01:04:01,066
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

985
01:04:01,866 --> 01:04:03,799
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

986
01:04:17,306 --> 01:04:19,006
Dong Jin!

987
01:05:19,738 --> 01:05:21,702
Dong Jin!

988
01:05:21,702 --> 01:05:24,799
What if you run into your husband?

989
01:05:24,799 --> 01:05:27,446
Tae Seong, what do I do?

990
01:05:27,446 --> 01:05:29,594
You should get out of there for now.

991
01:05:29,594 --> 01:05:32,999
The area was huge, so I'm not sure
we covered every route.

992
01:05:32,999 --> 01:05:35,599
So we don't know
where something could come from.

993
01:05:35,599 --> 01:05:37,233
Guess what I found?

994
01:05:37,233 --> 01:05:39,502
Mommy.

995
01:05:39,502 --> 01:05:42,882
Dong Jin, the law isn't perfect.
And you know that, right?

996
01:05:42,882 --> 01:05:44,662
I'll do my job,

997
01:05:44,662 --> 01:05:45,818
[Resignation Letter]
so you do yours.

998
01:05:45,818 --> 01:05:47,310
You're a reporter.

999
01:05:47,310 --> 01:05:49,166
[An Exclusive, Kingfisher...]
My husband has his work to do,

1000
01:05:49,166 --> 01:05:51,733
and I have mine...

